{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שעיר עזים א' חטאת", :translit "se'ir izim echat chatat", :gloss "one goat of a sin-offering"} {:he "לכפר", :translit "lechaper", :gloss "to make atonement"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast with standard sin-offering formula: Yom Kippur's goat omits לכפר because the day itself atones"}], :frame {:text "Throughout Numbers 28–29, the recurring formula for sin-offerings includes the phrase 'one goat for a sin-offering to make atonement for you' (Numbers 28:15, 22, 30; 29:5). The goat offered on Yom HaKippurim is described in Numbers 29:11 without the phrase 'to make atonement.' The Mishnah states that Yom HaKippurim itself effects atonement, as it is written 'for on this day shall atonement be made for you' (Leviticus 16:30) — hence the goat does not need its own atoning language since the day covers it.", :sources ["Mishnah Yoma 8:8" "Leviticus 16:30"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast with standard sin-offering formula: Yom Kippur's goat omits לכפר because the day itself atones", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:31:59.546641253Z", :model "glm-5.2"}